cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DigitalFly, please cite it as below. Please also cite the
  models and data it builds on (the references below), and follow the
  licenses of the data you use: all FlyWire-derived data is CC BY-NC 4.0,
  for non-commercial use only (see docs/ATTRIBUTION.md).
type: software
title: DigitalFly
abstract: >-
  A local, inspectable sensorimotor workbench: a physics-simulated fruit fly
  (FlyGym / NeuroMechFly on MuJoCo) walks toward what it sees, steered by an
  engineered six-unit controller or by FlyWire v783 connectome circuits with
  rate or spiking dynamics on the CPU or an optional GPU backend, with
  optional FlyVis eyes, per-side cell-type interventions, matched-seed
  experiments, exact and verifiable replay, a validation scorecard against
  published perturbation results, a connectivity explorer with Neuroglancer
  links, provenance manifests and NWB export, a research toolkit with an
  assumption-sensitivity analysis, a comparison with a recorded fly, an MCP
  server for AI agents and a plugin API. Results describe these models, not
  validated fly biology.
authors:
  - alias: Jeevash23
version: 0.7.0
date-released: '2026-11-13'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Jeevash23/frankenfly'
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - NeuroMechFly
  - FlyGym
  - MuJoCo
  - computational neuroscience
  - sensorimotor control
  - neuromechanical simulation
